# ---- B: the single-clock mixer (codex), Dart reference first, Kotlin parity second ----
MIX = ("Backing mixer contract (identical in Dart and Kotlin). Class BackingMixer(sampleRate). load(stems: Int16 arrays, one mono stem per instrument group, each covering the whole song; renderBpm; ticksPerBar; intervalMicros). A song bar b starts at stem sample barStartFrame(bar: b, epochFrame 0). "
"mix(out, chunkStart, engineBpm, epochFrame, ticksPerBar, intervalMicros) ADDS stem*gain/32768 into out for absolute frames [chunkStart, chunkStart+out.length). Audible only while |renderBpm-engineBpm|<0.001 and intervalMicros equal; else silence. "
"command(token, kind launch|stop, fromBar, bars, loop, atBar): transport bar t starts at barStartFrame(t, epochFrame). A command takes effect at the start of transport bar atBar (queued before that: emit state queued). For t>=atBar the song bar is fromBar+((t-atBar) mod bars) if loop, fromBar+(t-atBar) while < fromBar+bars otherwise (then stopped). Within transport bar t, frame f maps to stem sample songBarStart(songBar)+(f-barStart(t)), zero-padded or truncated at the song bar's length (re-anchor every bar: drift can never exceed one frame). "
"A stop command with atBar stops at that bar start. setGain(stem, gain) ramps linearly over 5 ms. A change of epochFrame or engine intervalMicros between mix calls stops playback and emits state stopped(reason epoch). State callback: onState(token, state queued|playing|stopped, transportBar). ")
